[05:42:46] ## What was already on disk, and what I added
[05:42:46] The previous session had written `frontend/src/items/ItemIcon.vue`, its spec, the six consumer changes (Profit rows, detail heading, both "still to buy" lists, tree nodes, Bank/Materials), `icon-browser-smoke.mjs`, `icon-live-check.mjs`, `recordingProxy.mjs` and `upstream-proxy.mjs`. I verified all of it against the criteria and added what was missing:
[05:42:46] - **`frontend/scripts/profit-page-perf.mjs`** — AC 5 had no evidence at all; the other scripts' comments referenced a harness that didn't exist.
[05:42:46] - **One production line**: `HttpIconImageFetcher`'s default client now uses `.proxy(ProxySelector.getDefault())`. Without it the JVM's proxy settings are ignored, so no upstream image request could be *counted or refused* — AC 4's upstream evidence would have had to be inferred. Behaviour is unchanged when no proxy is configured; covered by a new test that fetches an unresolvable host through a fixture proxy.
[05:42:46] ## Three defects fixed
[05:42:46] 1. `account-browser-smoke.mjs` demanded a bank reload produce exactly one request — item images now accompany it (failed on the first real-data run).
[05:42:46] 2. `icon-live-check.mjs` revalidated with `page.reload()`, which doesn't revalidate a fresh subresource, so it asserted on an empty list.
[05:42:46] 3. My own first perf run mis-attributed one opening's lazy-loading tail to the next, and treated a same-hash `goto` as a document load; both fixed before any number was recorded.
[05:42:46] ## Evidence
[05:42:46] - `smoke:icons` 10 steps, `smoke:profit` 30, `smoke:account` 8 (real data: 504 material images, all on the icon route, all no-referrer).
[05:42:46] - Live checks: 43 real images with the documented headers; reopening re-requested **0 of 43**; **12/12** `If-None-Match` → **304**; a **restarted** backend served 41 images with **0 upstream tunnels**; behind a *refusing* proxy (proven armed first by an independent CONNECT) stored images still rendered with **0 tunnels**.
[05:42:46] - §33 reverified across all three cache combinations against the real database: maxima **2 979 / 3 694 / 3 571 ms**, all inside 7 000 ms, with the complete requested set (**3 176 of 3 176** rows) in the DOM and no visible image left pending. Cold caches used isolated profiles and an isolated `ICON_CACHE_DIR` — the user's own cache was never touched.
[05:42:46] - Frontend 230 tests pass, build clean; backend icon suites `Tests run: 84, Failures: 0 — BUILD SUCCESS`.
[05:42:46] Limits are recorded explicitly rather than smoothed over: in-app renavigation isn't a comparable reopening (the client keeps the rows), offscreen icons keep loading after completion (counted, not waited out), a CONNECT count is tunnels not requests, revalidation used the browser's validate mode rather than a waited-out 24-hour window, and the selection detail is still untimed. **No performance acceptance, Phase 5 closure or health-review substitute is claimed.**
[05:42:46] I also stopped two leftover backends and a dev server the interrupted attempt had left listening, and confirmed every port I used is released while the user's own backend on 8080 still answers. Docs went into `CURRENT_ARCHITECTURE.md` only; story file, BACKLOG, `CLAUDE_RESULT.md` and `tasks/lessons.md` are updated. Nothing was committed.
